  "ablation_size_label": "scored case: 10.49M bytes, 10% contention (ranking_by LAST)",
  "takeaways": [
    "**Only the last benchmark is scored:** kernelbot's `LeaderboardTask.ranking_by` defaults to `RankCriterion.LAST`, and `histogram_py/task.yml` does not override it, so the leaderboard score is the 10.49M-byte / 10%-contention case alone (popcorn still labels it \"Geomean\"). Evidence: L4's 63.44 µs matches its 10.49M time (63.49 µs) while its 6-case geomean is 27.98 µs. Consequences: contention never enters the score, and small-size wins do not count. `--mode benchmark` also times only that one case.",
    "**Single-Launch Last-Man Global Bin Reduction + 128-Bit `uint4` Run-of-4 Collapse (`histogram_lastman_u4_cs256.crisp`):** Replacing the two-launch `output.zero_()` + scalar `uchar` shared-memory baseline (`22.5 µs` on H100) with a single-launch Last-Man pattern (`partials[0..255]` + `ticket` reset to 0 by the last CTA via `atomic-xchg!`), 128-bit `uint4` (16 bytes/load) vectorization, and a per-word Run-of-4 check (`(= w (* (logand w 255u) 16843009u))` -> single `atomic-add! +4u`) cut H100 10 MB runtime by **5.8 µs (−25.8%)** down to **16.7 ± 0.03 µs** (**14.90 µs public geomean**).",
    "**Grid sizing at the scored size:** bytes/thread matters more than replication count. At 10.49M on H100, 128 B/thread = 15.10 µs vs 16.29 µs at 256 B/thread (CTA count capped by 2xSMs) and 17.73 µs at 64 B/thread; L4 prefers 256. The size-adaptive entries (steps 2b/3b) moved B200 from 17.09 to 16.38 µs; on H100 and A100 the leaderboard runs landed within machine-to-machine noise (H100 public/secret swapped between runs, ~±10%).",
    "**Where the time goes (H100, scored case, per-case diagnostic):** empty-kernel floor 4.96 µs; raw uint4 read of the input 10.9 µs; + shared-memory zero/sync/reduce/merge structure ~1.9 µs; + shared atomics ~2.4 µs = 15.2 µs. Hand-written nvcc read kernels take the same ~10.5-11 µs as Crisp's loop, so Crisp's codegen is not the gap. Fence strength (`membar.gl` vs `fence.acq_rel.gpu`) and the last-man tail cost ~0; unroll 8 is slower; cache hints save ~0.2 µs. #1 (8.89 µs) beats a plain read of the input by ~2 µs.",
    "**Negative results:** warp aggregation (`match.any`/ballot) cannot help the scored 10%-contention case (a conflict-free probe ceiling was ~0.4 µs even on the full 6-case mix). Per-thread private uchar counters with no atomics (correct, lane-own-bank layout, 64 KB smem) were slower: 17.4 vs 15.2 µs; one shared atomic per byte beats a shared load + store per byte.",
    "**Hardware Bit-Field Extraction (`bfe.u32`) via Power-of-2 Division:** Writing byte extraction in Crisp as `(logand (/ w 256u) 255u)` and `(logand (/ w 65536u) 255u)` lowers directly through LLVM NVPTX to single-instruction hardware bit-field extracts (`bfe.u32 %r, %w, 8, 8` and `bfe.u32 %r, %w, 16, 8`), whereas `(ash w -8)` invokes the variable-shift helper `__crisp_ash_uint`.",
    "**Compiler bugs found:** BUG 139 (`=> nil` def-function whose `if` mixes a value branch and a void branch emits `store void`; llc fails), BUG 138 (on PTX, `ash`/`popcount` lower to `noinline` helper calls, hence the `(/ w 256u)` idiom above), BUG 140 (CUDA hoist sizes uchar/ushort shared scratch at 4 bytes/element). All in `plan/bugs.md`."
